Question Title: Simplify the Compilation Process
Question Link: https://my.newtonschool.co/playground/code/9kh4giios2j4?lecture_hash=t5qc0u6ap8tg

Solution:
touch build.sh
echo "#!/bin/bash" > build.sh
echo "gcc hello.c -o hello" >> build.sh
chmod +x build.sh
./build.sh
./hello

Approach:
1. Created build.sh and wrote the shebang line as its first line so it runs with bash.
2. Added the command gcc hello.c -o hello with >> so the shebang was kept. This compiles hello.c into an executable named hello.
3. Gave the script execute permission with chmod +x.
4. Ran ./build.sh to compile, then ./hello, which printed Hello from C.